WEBVTT

03:04.268 --> 03:06.354
Tod's father called.

03:06.479 --> 03:10.691
They'll pick you up tomorrow at 3:30, the bus leaves around 5.

03:11.025 --> 03:16.238
—Was my suitcase enough for you? —No, you have to leave that.

03:17.239 --> 03:21.786
I've already flown with that tag without anything happening,

03:21.952 --> 03:25.623
so I'd say it's better if it stays attached to the suitcase.

03:25.748 --> 03:29.877
-Let's say it brings luck. -Where does such a stupid idea come from?

03:30.628 --> 03:32.713
Well, I'm still alive.

03:36.759 --> 03:42.139
17 years old, a 10-day trip to Paris with

03:42.264 --> 03:45.226
school friends, without parents, in spring...

03:45.768 --> 03:49.730
Enjoy it, Alex. Life is all yours.

04:56.422 --> 05:00.050
Parking is prohibited in the area marked in white.

05:00.217 --> 05:05.139
Stopping is permitted only for loading and unloading baggage.

05:09.101 --> 05:13.147
—Oh, Hitchcock. -What's up? -I'll give you a hand. Done.

05:13.606 --> 05:16.650
—What an idiot.  -Good job.

05:17.902 --> 05:20.654
-You left this above. -Thank you.

05:20.821 --> 05:25.159
-Get your bags. -Hi, Christa. Hi, Blake.

05:25.576 --> 05:28.412
-What are you doing? -He tries.

05:28.537 --> 05:31.582
-So, have you taken everything? -Yes, dad.

05:35.794 --> 05:40.257
-What did he say? To go? -I do not know.

05:40.966 --> 05:45.513
-These are for both of us. And have fun. -Thanks Dad.

05:45.638 --> 05:50.100
-For both. -Let's go. —Keep an eye on them. -Certain.

05:59.235 --> 06:02.947
I didn't think I'd look worse here than in the school album photo.

06:03.113 --> 06:05.616
Think of me seeing you every day.

06:14.375 --> 06:16.210
What the fuck does he want?

06:21.549 --> 06:23.717
The airport is not responsible for beggars.

06:30.641 --> 06:33.143
Flight 406, boarding immediately.

06:33.310 --> 06:36.313
Death is not the end.

06:37.898 --> 06:43.320
-For you yes if you bother my students. -Hare Rama. -Fuck you.

06:48.492 --> 06:53.163
Sorry, but I have to ask you some questions. Did you pack your bags?

06:53.289 --> 06:58.002
Did he always have them with you or did he entrust them to someone else?

07:00.629 --> 07:04.258
—Mr. Browning?  -No.

07:04.842 --> 07:09.346
Wasn't she entrusted with anything by people unknown to her?

07:21.817 --> 07:27.448
-Like her birthday. -What? -September, 25. 9 and 25.

07:27.573 --> 07:31.493
The digits of her birthday are the same as the departure time.

07:43.505 --> 07:45.799
What a drag.

07:46.717 --> 07:50.846
—Dad said it's for both of us. Give me some. —Don't break.

07:50.971 --> 07:54.808
-Give me something. -Stop that! - Get it over with. -Excuse me.

07:56.018 --> 07:58.062
You're an idiot.

08:08.405 --> 08:09.990
-Thank you. -Not at all.

08:39.395 --> 08:42.356
Alex, shall we go take a shit?

08:42.815 --> 08:48.862
-Can't you go alone? -Think. We embark on a 7 hour flight,

08:48.987 --> 08:52.908
the toilets on the plane are lockers without ventilation.

08:53.075 --> 08:57.204
Let's say halfway through the flight you have to unload some junk food.

08:57.371 --> 08:59.957
Dropped 1.3kg of stuff without the parachute.

09:00.124 --> 09:03.961
A moment later Christa or Blake enters.

09:04.420 --> 09:07.965
Do you want them to associate their glassy, ​​horrified

09:08.132 --> 09:12.261
gaze with that disgusted grin that curls their mouth?

09:31.155 --> 09:33.157
He died in a plane crash.

09:33.323 --> 09:35.993
Ladies and gentlemen, thank you for your patience.

09:36.118 --> 09:40.831
We can begin boarding operations for flight 180 to Paris.

09:40.956 --> 09:43.083
Exit 46.

09:50.674 --> 09:53.969
Flight 180 to Paris, immediate boarding, exit 46.

09:54.094 --> 09:56.930
Has anyone seen Billy Hitchcock?

10:04.688 --> 10:06.523
Go.

10:32.716 --> 10:36.720
Go. Ouch, you hurt me.

10:54.154 --> 10:58.909
That's a good sign, it would take a crazy God to bring this plane down.

11:04.331 --> 11:05.999
A truly crazy God.

11:09.253 --> 11:13.966
-HI. -Hi, Tod. -Hello, how is he doing? -Is this your place? -Yes, yours is that.

11:29.398 --> 11:32.860
-Tod, can you change places with Christa? -Oh, damn.

11:33.026 --> 11:38.198
Gladly, but I have a bladder problem, an infection.

11:38.365 --> 11:41.618
-Come on, let's ask Alex. -Let's try with him.

11:50.043 --> 11:54.548
Can you switch places with Blake so we're close? Tod doesn't want it.

11:57.259 --> 12:00.137
-Please. -Yes.

12:04.099 --> 12:08.562
-You are so cute. Thank you. -Thank you.

12:09.187 --> 12:11.398
It is a pleasure.

12:11.523 --> 12:13.650
Homosexual!

12:16.028 --> 12:20.240
Were you convinced we were touching his tits over Greenland?

12:20.365 --> 12:24.578
Anyway, because of you I'll have to watch Stuart Little.

12:26.413 --> 12:29.583
Thank you, you are a friend, I love you.

12:32.169 --> 12:36.006
-Sorry, I'm late. My place is there. -Please.

12:36.131 --> 12:39.343
-Will you let me in? -HI. -Okay, I'll go around.

12:39.509 --> 12:44.181
Prepare for takeoff. Illustrate the on-board safety systems.

12:44.306 --> 12:48.852
To fasten the seat belts correctly, insert the white part

12:48.977 --> 12:54.316
into the buckle. To unfasten them, lift the mobile part.

12:56.526 --> 12:59.363
Prepare for takeoff.

13:44.491 --> 13:46.493
And go!

13:52.165 --> 13:53.750
Let's go.

14:06.346 --> 14:08.348
Everything is fine.

14:50.348 --> 14:54.561
Quick, put on your masks! Hurry up.

15:19.753 --> 15:21.421
The hand.

15:44.152 --> 15:48.615
Alex, can you switch places with Blake so we're close?

15:48.782 --> 15:53.370
—I asked Tod, but he says he has a health problem. -Please.

15:53.495 --> 15:57.624
We invite passengers to take their seats and fasten their seat belts.

16:00.043 --> 16:02.212
What's happening to you?

16:05.048 --> 16:07.050
-Is there any problem? -Yes, to the brain.

16:09.010 --> 16:11.805
-What's up? That the plane is about to explode! -Don't shoot them.

16:11.930 --> 16:14.599
-You are not funny. -If you want to joke, it's not funny.

16:14.724 --> 16:18.645
-It's not a joke! -Stay calm. -Now you broke me.

16:18.770 --> 16:22.065
-It will explode. -We'll let you off if you continue. -I'll handle that. -Take it easy.

16:22.232 --> 16:26.444
-I'm leaving. -Stay still. - Leave him.

16:26.570 --> 16:29.906
-Sorry, that's my place. -Let me get off. - Leave him.

16:30.073 --> 16:34.286
-He had nothing to do with it. -The plane will explode! -Stay in your seats.

16:34.411 --> 16:37.330
It will explode. You all have to get out.

16:37.497 --> 16:40.167
Go and see what they do to him.

16:49.676 --> 16:54.431
-I did nothing. -Take your hands off me. -Stop it, idiot.

16:54.931 --> 16:59.352
-Floor. —So, is that clear? These do not go back on board. —And leave me.

16:59.477 --> 17:03.607
Wait, I have 40 guys going to Paris, please.

17:03.773 --> 17:08.195
-I know, but understand my position. -I understand, but one of us has to go up,

17:08.361 --> 17:12.782
we cannot leave them in Paris without teachers. -Carter, no!

17:12.908 --> 17:16.286
Just stand there.  Stay there!

17:16.453 --> 17:18.538
One of you can get back up, no one else.

17:18.705 --> 17:23.043
Last call for flight 371 to London. Immediate boarding.

17:23.168 --> 17:25.921
The airline picks up one of us.

17:26.046 --> 17:28.798
The others can take the 11am flight, it will arrive...

17:28.924 --> 17:34.387
-I'll stay. -No, you speak French, take it yourself, it's better.

17:34.721 --> 17:38.558
I was in the bathroom and the door got stuck and I couldn't...

17:39.100 --> 17:43.563
Wait, I didn't argue with anyone. What a drag.

17:44.856 --> 17:46.483
Thank you.

17:50.862 --> 17:53.907
I called your parents, they're on their way.

17:58.620 --> 18:00.247
Goodbye Paris.

18:03.500 --> 18:08.255
-Tell me. Tell me what happened. -I saw it.

18:08.630 --> 18:13.885
I saw it on the runway, I saw it take off.

18:14.052 --> 18:17.597
—From the window I could see the lights of the airport. -No, Carter.

18:17.722 --> 18:21.101
The fuselage begins to shake and the left side breaks.

18:21.268 --> 18:26.273
And the whole plane explodes. It was so real, like it was really happening.

18:26.398 --> 18:30.527
-Have you been on many planes that have exploded? -You must have fallen asleep.

18:30.652 --> 18:34.906
They kicked us off the plane, we lost half a day in Paris and

18:35.031 --> 18:40.287
just because he had a bad dream?! The plane is about to explode!

18:40.453 --> 18:44.374
—Stop it! —You make the trip to the hospital.

18:45.333 --> 18:48.878
Alex, stop it!

18:52.716 --> 18:55.468
He goes away and we stay.

18:57.345 --> 19:01.891
-You pay for this. -I wish you were on the plane. You bad ass!

19:02.058 --> 19:03.601
Oh, fuck!

20:05.580 --> 20:07.957
You look at me like it's my fault.

20:11.628 --> 20:13.880
I have nothing to do with it.

20:16.758 --> 20:18.718
Are there any survivors?

20:23.973 --> 20:26.059
I do not know.

20:29.020 --> 20:33.400
-You think I'm some kind of.. .-he's not a sorcerer.

20:38.113 --> 20:41.574
I'm Howard Segal, Transportation Security Agency.

20:41.699 --> 20:45.620
We have warned your parents, they are coming.

20:46.329 --> 20:52.585
Meanwhile, is there anyone who needs medical or spiritual assistance?

20:52.710 --> 20:55.839
What happened? Are there any survivors?

20:58.216 --> 21:00.844
The cause of the explosion is still unspecified.

21:00.969 --> 21:05.056
The county authorities are at work, the searches continue,

21:05.181 --> 21:09.769
let's hope that... -Excuse me. I'm Agent Weine, this is Agent Schreck.

21:09.936 --> 21:14.941
We're FBI. I can imagine how you feel and I know it

21:15.066 --> 21:18.778
won't be easy, but we have to ask you some questions,

21:18.903 --> 21:21.281
while the memories are still fresh.

21:21.448 --> 21:26.369
They will certainly be useful for rescue operations and judicial investigations.

21:30.039 --> 21:33.793
You said, "You have to get off, the plane is about to explode."

21:33.918 --> 21:38.465
-How did you know? -I had a feeling.

21:40.049 --> 21:43.803
-A strange feeling. -Did you take any sedatives before boarding?

21:43.970 --> 21:47.640
Once on board, you took sleeping pills, narcotics, hallucinogens...

21:47.807 --> 21:53.021
-Have you taken drugs? -No. I saw it.

21:55.690 --> 21:59.402
I saw the plane explode.

21:59.527 --> 22:03.156
Does the strange feeling have anything to do with what you said?

22:03.323 --> 22:07.452
That you wanted Carter Horton to be on that plane before it exploded?

22:09.162 --> 22:13.500
-Then why did you say that? -I didn't think it would really happen.

22:13.666 --> 22:18.254
If so, why did you want to get off the plane?

22:22.050 --> 22:27.847
My brother George told me to see what happened to Alex.

22:28.765 --> 22:32.018
So he stayed...

22:38.233 --> 22:40.860
He told me to get off the plane.

22:41.152 --> 22:46.115
Larry Murnau said he wanted to stay, but I told

22:46.241 --> 22:51.454
him he had to go. I sent him back on the plane.

22:53.957 --> 22:58.962
So, they didn't force you to leave the plane, you

22:59.128 --> 23:02.632
said you weren't friends with those who got off,

23:02.757 --> 23:05.385
can you explain to us why you came down?

23:06.177 --> 23:08.930
Because I saw and heard Alex.

23:14.269 --> 23:16.396
And I believed him.

23:27.490 --> 23:30.743
—Oh, God, Alex!  —A|ex, my son.

23:33.705 --> 23:35.999
Oh, Terry, my child.

23:38.001 --> 23:41.921
-There he is. -How are you?

24:06.195 --> 24:08.364
Thanks for the ride.

25:10.927 --> 25:16.432
This is the first piece to reach the shore of the wreckage of Flight 180,

25:16.557 --> 25:21.688
which exploded shortly after take-off at 9.25pm ​​from JFK in New York.

25:21.813 --> 25:24.357
At the moment there are no survivors.

25:24.482 --> 25:29.028
The efforts of the coast guard and rescue teams continue,

25:29.153 --> 25:33.282
despite the difficulties caused by the burning fuel patches.

25:33.408 --> 25:36.953
The authorities say they are pessimistic about the possibility

25:37.120 --> 25:42.959
of finding any survivors. They are all presumed dead.

25:43.084 --> 25:46.963
Among them, 40 students and 4 teachers

25:47.130 --> 25:50.800
who had gone on a school trip to Paris.

25:50.925 --> 25:56.055
Some students were reportedly dropped off before takeoff.

25:56.222 --> 26:00.810
The authorities prefer not to say too much about the causes.

26:00.977 --> 26:05.565
Investigators from the Transportation Security Agency and

26:05.690 --> 26:09.152
the FBI arrived at the airport to begin the investigation.

26:09.444 --> 26:15.074
Eyewitnesses reported seeing the plane explode.

26:15.533 --> 26:19.912
At the time, no other aircraft were visible near Flight 180.

26:20.037 --> 26:24.167
The airport and air traffic controllers confirm the witnesses' version.

26:24.292 --> 26:29.005
After the explosion fragments would have rained into the Atlantic.

26:55.239 --> 27:01.370
It has been 39 days since we lost our 39 friends and teachers. And

27:01.496 --> 27:07.877
every day that passes without knowing the causes of the disaster

27:08.044 --> 27:11.547
we ask ourselves: why?

27:11.839 --> 27:16.886
Ecclesiastes tells us: "Man does not even know

27:17.011 --> 27:20.890
his time, like fish caught in the fatal net,

27:21.015 --> 27:23.142
or birds caught in a snare...

27:23.267 --> 27:28.731
Like these, the man is surprised by the misfortune that suddenly

27:28.856 --> 27:35.988
befalls him. And so in order to heal and escape the presence of death,

27:36.155 --> 27:42.328
we must cry and remember them with this monument.

28:27.081 --> 28:31.544
Don't think I'm grateful just because my name isn't on there.

28:32.169 --> 28:35.214
-At all. -If I have a debt, it is with them.

28:35.548 --> 28:39.802
-Live my life to the fullest. -Then stay away from alcohol.

28:41.012 --> 28:44.807
Don't tell me what to do. I control my life, not you.

28:48.936 --> 28:51.063
I will never die.

28:59.363 --> 29:06.245
Hey, Alex, listen. The other day I went to take the driving test.

29:06.412 --> 29:09.916
I got a 70, which is a poor score, but I passed.

29:10.041 --> 29:13.753
When I finish the exam, you know the guy in the car who examines you?

29:13.920 --> 29:19.008
-Certain. -He said to me: "Young man, you will die very young."

29:23.012 --> 29:25.014
Well, is it true?

29:25.181 --> 29:27.850
Not now and not here.  He is excluded.

29:30.853 --> 29:35.274
-If I ask Silvia Paster out, will she say no? -Fuck.

29:35.650 --> 29:38.110
-Okay.  -Already.  -Already.

29:45.660 --> 29:49.622
—Mrs Lewton? -Please, it terrifies me to hear you talk.

29:50.873 --> 29:52.875
Excuse me.

30:00.758 --> 30:03.594
-HI. -HI.

30:05.221 --> 30:10.309
Don't get any strange ideas, but I miss you. Really.

30:10.768 --> 30:13.646
Yes, you too.

30:14.689 --> 30:18.734
-But my father doesn't understand, you know. -Already.

30:20.403 --> 30:24.156
Once he gets over this, we'll get the car

30:24.490 --> 30:30.413
and we go to town to watch the Yankees. -Yes, certainly.

30:34.917 --> 30:39.422
I'd better go. Lewton had given me some material in

30:39.588 --> 30:43.426
class, I'll read that. She tells how I feel inside.

30:45.928 --> 30:48.264
We will see each other.

30:56.856 --> 30:59.608
It's thanks to you that I'm still alive.

31:02.194 --> 31:03.654
Thank you.

31:10.494 --> 31:15.458
We say that the time of death cannot be predicted.

31:15.583 --> 31:21.297
But when we say this, we imagine that

31:21.464 --> 31:24.216
hour lies in a dark and distant future.

31:25.009 --> 31:30.473
The idea that it has a connection with the day that has begun does not even remotely occur to us.

31:31.432 --> 31:34.894
Or that death may come this very afternoon.

31:36.020 --> 31:39.398
This afternoon that seems so certain to us,

31:39.982 --> 31:44.320
which has every hour already established and programmed.

36:12.463 --> 36:17.009
The Lakers have a solid lead at this point.

37:28.914 --> 37:32.543
What happened?  Where's Tod?

37:38.757 --> 37:40.884
Go away.

37:54.565 --> 37:57.025
-You didn't see it coming. -What happened?

37:57.151 --> 38:01.947
You had triggered such guilt in Tod for

38:02.072 --> 38:05.409
leaving George that he committed suicide.

38:08.245 --> 38:10.998
He would never have done it.

38:11.123 --> 38:14.793
He said we'd see each other again when he got over her.

38:14.960 --> 38:18.422
Why would he tell me these things if he was thinking of killing himself?!

38:25.888 --> 38:29.224
Come on, close.  We can go.

39:17.356 --> 39:21.193
—It's almost autumn. —We are still in June.

39:24.112 --> 39:26.281
Yes, but everything is always in transition.

39:26.448 --> 39:30.661
If you concentrate, even now that it's summer you can feel autumn.

39:31.286 --> 39:36.500
-I like being able to see the future. -Why were you outside Tod's house yesterday?

39:40.087 --> 39:44.216
I've watched enough TV to know that the FBI doesn't investigate teen suicides.

39:44.383 --> 39:46.385
If they were there yesterday, it means that:

39:46.552 --> 39:49.805
1) they don't know what caused the disaster 2) they don't rule anything out.

39:49.972 --> 39:54.101
The fact that 7 people got off the plane is undoubtedly strange.

39:54.226 --> 39:58.272
If you then add that one of those had a vision of the plane exploding

39:58.397 --> 40:02.150
shortly before it actually exploded, it's pretty suspicious.

40:02.276 --> 40:06.488
And the fact that the visionary's friend just committed suicide doesn't help.

40:06.989 --> 40:09.741
Why were you there last night?

40:14.871 --> 40:20.586
-Do you know what this is? -It's a...

40:23.880 --> 40:27.718
-Who is this glass head? -It's you.

40:29.052 --> 40:33.724
It's not a portrait, it's how you make me feel.

40:36.435 --> 40:42.441
-I am sorry. -Like you, this sculpture doesn't really know what it is and why.

40:43.525 --> 40:47.779
He refuses to take shape and at the same time

40:47.904 --> 40:51.033
creates a strong, but incomprehensible attraction.

40:53.619 --> 40:57.289
In four years of school we never said a word to each other.

40:57.414 --> 41:00.834
But at some point on the plane I felt what you felt.

41:01.251 --> 41:03.420
I didn't understand where those emotions

41:03.587 --> 41:05.881
came from until you started acting crazy.

41:06.006 --> 41:10.886
I didn't see what you saw, but I felt it too.

41:11.053 --> 41:16.141
You I still try, don't you? Something from that day is still inside you.

41:18.727 --> 41:21.146
I know because I keep hearing you.

41:23.857 --> 41:25.984
That's why I was there last night.

41:28.695 --> 41:31.865
It's the first time I've dealt with death.

41:31.990 --> 41:34.701
It could all be in our heads.

41:35.661 --> 41:39.247
-But the feeling is that it is around us. -Meaning what?

41:42.709 --> 41:47.172
What if Tod had just been the first of us?

41:48.173 --> 41:54.763
-Is that something you feel? -I don't know. If at least I could see him again,

41:54.888 --> 41:57.933
one last time, I would know maybe.

41:59.476 --> 42:02.187
So, let's go to him.

42:35.929 --> 42:38.306
It is exciting.

42:39.599 --> 42:44.146
-This place? -Doing something we shouldn't do.

42:47.774 --> 42:49.651
Let's go.

43:09.129 --> 43:14.760
-And he? -I believe. Why did they make him up like Michael Jackson?

43:15.677 --> 43:21.266
Yes, it's him, but there's nothing left of Tod except his body.

43:24.895 --> 43:26.438
Christ!

43:26.938 --> 43:32.778
Shh, please, you will wake the dead man.

43:44.122 --> 43:46.666
-Why did he move? -Chemical substances.

43:46.833 --> 43:51.046
Introducing them into the vascular system can cause spasms.

43:51.797 --> 43:56.468
-Look, I'm a friend of his... -I know who you are.

43:58.345 --> 44:00.722
How do you explain all those signs?

44:00.889 --> 44:05.727
-Skin tears from pulling the thread. -For pulling the thread?

44:06.186 --> 44:09.981
So he didn't want to kill himself, it was an accident.

44:10.148 --> 44:16.238
In death there are no accidents, no coincidences, no setbacks.

44:16.363 --> 44:18.824
And there are no loopholes.

44:20.325 --> 44:23.995
What you need to understand is that we are

44:24.120 --> 44:26.498
all little mice held by the tail by a cat.

44:26.623 --> 44:30.752
Our every gesture, action, from the most banal to the

44:30.919 --> 44:34.047
most noble, the red light at which we stop or not,

44:34.214 --> 44:36.842
the people we have sex with or not,

44:36.967 --> 44:40.053
the planes we travel on and get off,

44:40.220 --> 44:45.684
everything is part of Death's sadistic plan, which leads to the grave.

44:46.643 --> 44:48.520
A drawing?

44:49.521 --> 44:53.859
Does that mean that if you understand the plan you can fool Death?

44:56.611 --> 44:59.698
You already did it when you got off that plane.

45:00.657 --> 45:06.371
Your friend's end proves that Death has a new plan for you.

45:07.581 --> 45:12.878
So now you have to figure out when and how she will come back for you.

45:13.753 --> 45:19.175
Use your intuition if you want to try to get out of it.

45:19.301 --> 45:24.139
But keep in mind the risk of blowing up the plan, of

45:24.306 --> 45:28.560
not adapting to the plan. You might go on a rampage

45:28.727 --> 45:32.772
that would terrify even the grim reaper.

45:34.065 --> 45:37.903
And there's no point pissing off that old slut.

45:42.073 --> 45:46.912
Agree. So, sorry for the inconvenience.

45:47.078 --> 45:50.415
No disturbances.  No excuses.

45:54.169 --> 45:55.712
We will see each other soon.

46:02.427 --> 46:05.764
